Chat Widget HTML Elements

Add these three HTML elements to any page where you want the chatbot
to appear (index.html, dashboard.html, contact.html).

Step 1 — Add the HTML elements (inside <main> or wherever you want the chat):

<input id="chat-input" type="text" placeholder="Ask us anything..." />
<button id="chat-send">Send</button>
<div id="chat-reply"></div>

Step 2 — Add the script tag (at the bottom of <body>, before </body>):

<script src="/chat-widget.js"></script>

How it works:
- The customer types a message into #chat-input and clicks Send (or
presses Enter)
- The widget POSTs the message to /api/chat
- The reply from the chatbot appears in chat-reply
- While waiting, it shows 'Thinking...'
- On error it shows a friendly fallback message

The chat-widget.js file is already in your GitHub repo.
The /api/chat backend is powered by api/index.py (FastAPI + CrewAI
+ Firebase).
